{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your skills live in S3, a database, or a private registry, not on disk. To feed\nthem to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSkills"},{"type":"text","value":", implement a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SkillSource"},{"type":"text","value":". It is a small, bytes-only\ninterface, so it works anywhere, including the edge."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This page shows the minimum source, then how to prove it is correct with the\nconformance suite that ships in the package."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-minimum-source","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The minimum source"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A source needs two methods: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"list"},{"type":"text","value":" returns the catalog, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"load"},{"type":"text","value":" returns one\nskill's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SKILL.md"},{"type":"text","value":" body. Here is an S3-backed one."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { SkillSource } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\n\nexport function s3Skills(bucket: S3Bucket): SkillSource {\n  return {\n    async list() {\n      const index = await bucket.getJSON('skills/index.json')\n      return index.map((s) => ({ name: s.name, description: s.description }))\n    },\n    async load(name) {\n      return bucket.getText(`skills/${name}/SKILL.md`)\n    },\n  }\n}","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass it straight to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSkills(s3Skills(bucket))"},{"type":"text","value":". The middleware strips the\nfrontmatter from what "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"load"},{"type":"text","value":" returns, so return the raw "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SKILL.md"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"add-resources-and-a-revision","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add resources and a revision"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two optional methods make the source better:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"revision()"},{"type":"text","value":" returns a stable string that changes only when content changes.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSkills"},{"type":"text","value":" lists once per "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call and does not cache on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"revision()"},{"type":"text","value":".\nAdd it so combinators, your own cache, or a later catalog memo can key on it\n(a bucket ETag, a content hash)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listResources"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"readResource"},{"type":"text","value":" expose a skill's bundled files so\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"read_skill_resource"},{"type":"text","value":" can read them."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { SkillSource } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\n\nexport function s3Skills(bucket: S3Bucket): SkillSource {\n  return {\n    revision: () => bucket.getText('skills/index.etag'),\n    async list() {\n      /* as above */\n    },\n    async load(name) {\n      return bucket.getText(`skills/${name}/SKILL.md`)\n    },\n    async listResources(name) {\n      return bucket.listKeys(`skills/${name}/references/`)\n    },\n    async readResource(name, path) {\n      return bucket.getBytes(`skills/${name}/${path}`)\n    },\n  }\n}","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The source is bytes only on purpose. There is no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"path"},{"type":"text","value":" field, so a database or\nregistry source is a first-class citizen, not a second-class one bolted onto a\nfilesystem assumption."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"prove-it-with-the-conformance-suite","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prove it with the conformance suite"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapter code is easy to get subtly wrong (a missing skill that returns empty\ninstead of throwing, a resource path that escapes the skill root). The package\nships a conformance suite so you test behavior, not guesswork."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Seed your source with the fixture the suite expects (a skill "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"alpha"},{"type":"text","value":" with a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"references/note.md"},{"type":"text","value":" resource whose contents are "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hello"},{"type":"text","value":", and a skill "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beta"},{"type":"text","value":"),\nthen run it:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { runSkillSourceConformance } from '@tanstack/ai-skills/testing'\nimport { s3Skills } from './s3-skills'\n\nrunSkillSourceConformance(() => s3Skills(makeTestBucket()), 's3')","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The suite checks the things that break in production:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a missing skill name throws, it does not return empty"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"resources load, and a path like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"../../etc/passwd"},{"type":"text","value":" is rejected"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"revision()"},{"type":"text","value":" is stable across identical content"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"concurrent "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"list()"},{"type":"text","value":" calls stay consistent"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"script bytes come back correctly (so your source keeps working when script\nexecution lands in a later release)"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If it passes, your source is safe to hand to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSkills"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"where-to-go-next","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Where to go next"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./skill-sources","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Skill sources"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — the built-in sources and the combinators."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./agent-skills","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Portable Agent Skills"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — the middleware and the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"load_skill"},{"type":"text","value":"\nflow your source feeds."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"the-minimum-source","text":"The minimum source","level":2},{"id":"add-resources-and-a-revision","text":"Add resources and a revision","level":2},{"id":"prove-it-with-the-conformance-suite","text":"Prove it with the conformance suite","level":2},{"id":"where-to-go-next","text":"Where to go next","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYour skills live in S3, a database, or a private registry, not on disk. To feed\nthem to `withSkills`, implement a `SkillSource`. It is a small, bytes-only\ninterface, so it works anywhere, including the edge.\n\nThis page shows the minimum source, then how to prove it is correct with the\nconformance suite that ships in the package.\n\n## The minimum source\n\nA source needs two methods: `list` returns the catalog, `load` returns one\nskill's `SKILL.md` body. Here is an S3-backed one.\n\n```ts ignore\nimport type { SkillSource } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\n\nexport function s3Skills(bucket: S3Bucket): SkillSource {\n  return {\n    async list() {\n      const index = await bucket.getJSON('skills/index.json')\n      return index.map((s) => ({ name: s.name, description: s.description }))\n    },\n    async load(name) {\n      return bucket.getText(`skills/${name}/SKILL.md`)\n    },\n  }\n}\n```\n\nPass it straight to `withSkills(s3Skills(bucket))`. The middleware strips the\nfrontmatter from what `load` returns, so return the raw `SKILL.md`.\n\n## Add resources and a revision\n\nTwo optional methods make the source better:\n\n- `revision()` returns a stable string that changes only when content changes.\n  `withSkills` lists once per `chat()` call and does not cache on `revision()`.\n  Add it so combinators, your own cache, or a later catalog memo can key on it\n  (a bucket ETag, a content hash).\n- `listResources` and `readResource` expose a skill's bundled files so\n  `read_skill_resource` can read them.\n\n```ts ignore\nimport type { SkillSource } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\n\nexport function s3Skills(bucket: S3Bucket): SkillSource {\n  return {\n    revision: () => bucket.getText('skills/index.etag'),\n    async list() {\n      /* as above */\n    },\n    async load(name) {\n      return bucket.getText(`skills/${name}/SKILL.md`)\n    },\n    async listResources(name) {\n      return bucket.listKeys(`skills/${name}/references/`)\n    },\n    async readResource(name, path) {\n      return bucket.getBytes(`skills/${name}/${path}`)\n    },\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe source is bytes only on purpose. There is no `path` field, so a database or\nregistry source is a first-class citizen, not a second-class one bolted onto a\nfilesystem assumption.\n\n## Prove it with the conformance suite\n\nAdapter code is easy to get subtly wrong (a missing skill that returns empty\ninstead of throwing, a resource path that escapes the skill root). The package\nships a conformance suite so you test behavior, not guesswork.\n\nSeed your source with the fixture the suite expects (a skill `alpha` with a\n`references/note.md` resource whose contents are `hello`, and a skill `beta`),\nthen run it:\n\n```ts ignore\nimport { runSkillSourceConformance } from '@tanstack/ai-skills/testing'\nimport { s3Skills } from './s3-skills'\n\nrunSkillSourceConformance(() => s3Skills(makeTestBucket()), 's3')\n```\n\nThe suite checks the things that break in production:\n\n- a missing skill name throws, it does not return empty\n- resources load, and a path like `../../etc/passwd` is rejected\n- `revision()` is stable across identical content\n- concurrent `list()` calls stay consistent\n- script bytes come back correctly (so your source keeps working when script\n  execution lands in a later release)\n\nIf it passes, your source is safe to hand to `withSkills`.\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- [Skill sources](./skill-sources) — the built-in sources and the combinators.\n- [Portable Agent Skills](./agent-skills) — the middleware and the `load_skill`\n  flow your source feeds.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Write a Skill Source\nid: writing-skill-sources\norder: 3\ndescription: \"Back portable Agent Skills with your own store (S3, a database, a registry) by implementing SkillSource, and prove it with the shipped conformance suite.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - SkillSource\n  - custom skill source\n  - conformance\n  - runSkillSourceConformance\n  - s3 skills\n  - database skills\n---\n\nYour skills live in S3, a database, or a private registry, not on disk. To feed\nthem to `withSkills`, implement a `SkillSource`. It is a small, bytes-only\ninterface, so it works anywhere, including the edge.\n\nThis page shows the minimum source, then how to prove it is correct with the\nconformance suite that ships in the package.\n\n## The minimum source\n\nA source needs two methods: `list` returns the catalog, `load` returns one\nskill's `SKILL.md` body. Here is an S3-backed one.\n\n```ts ignore\nimport type { SkillSource } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\n\nexport function s3Skills(bucket: S3Bucket): SkillSource {\n  return {\n    async list() {\n      const index = await bucket.getJSON('skills/index.json')\n      return index.map((s) => ({ name: s.name, description: s.description }))\n    },\n    async load(name) {\n      return bucket.getText(`skills/${name}/SKILL.md`)\n    },\n  }\n}\n```\n\nPass it straight to `withSkills(s3Skills(bucket))`. The middleware strips the\nfrontmatter from what `load` returns, so return the raw `SKILL.md`.\n\n## Add resources and a revision\n\nTwo optional methods make the source better:\n\n- `revision()` returns a stable string that changes only when content changes.\n  `withSkills` lists once per `chat()` call and does not cache on `revision()`.\n  Add it so combinators, your own cache, or a later catalog memo can key on it\n  (a bucket ETag, a content hash).\n- `listResources` and `readResource` expose a skill's bundled files so\n  `read_skill_resource` can read them.\n\n```ts ignore\nimport type { SkillSource } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\n\nexport function s3Skills(bucket: S3Bucket): SkillSource {\n  return {\n    revision: () => bucket.getText('skills/index.etag'),\n    async list() {\n      /* as above */\n    },\n    async load(name) {\n      return bucket.getText(`skills/${name}/SKILL.md`)\n    },\n    async listResources(name) {\n      return bucket.listKeys(`skills/${name}/references/`)\n    },\n    async readResource(name, path) {\n      return bucket.getBytes(`skills/${name}/${path}`)\n    },\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe source is bytes only on purpose. There is no `path` field, so a database or\nregistry source is a first-class citizen, not a second-class one bolted onto a\nfilesystem assumption.\n\n## Prove it with the conformance suite\n\nAdapter code is easy to get subtly wrong (a missing skill that returns empty\ninstead of throwing, a resource path that escapes the skill root). The package\nships a conformance suite so you test behavior, not guesswork.\n\nSeed your source with the fixture the suite expects (a skill `alpha` with a\n`references/note.md` resource whose contents are `hello`, and a skill `beta`),\nthen run it:\n\n```ts ignore\nimport { runSkillSourceConformance } from '@tanstack/ai-skills/testing'\nimport { s3Skills } from './s3-skills'\n\nrunSkillSourceConformance(() => s3Skills(makeTestBucket()), 's3')\n```\n\nThe suite checks the things that break in production:\n\n- a missing skill name throws, it does not return empty\n- resources load, and a path like `../../etc/passwd` is rejected\n- `revision()` is stable across identical content\n- concurrent `list()` calls stay consistent\n- script bytes come back correctly (so your source keeps working when script\n  execution lands in a later release)\n\nIf it passes, your source is safe to hand to `withSkills`.\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- [Skill sources](./skill-sources) — the built-in sources and the combinators.\n- [Portable Agent Skills](./agent-skills) — the middleware and the `load_skill`\n  flow your source feeds.\n"}
